-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Basalt lavas with interbedded agglomerate, conglomerate and sandstone. \r\n\r\nThe Basal Member occurs on Sanday. \r\n\r\nOn Canna, the Tighard Member, Cnoc Bhrostan Member, Carn a'Ghaill Member, Beul Lama Sgorr Member, and Eilean a'Bhàird Member are recognised. \r\n\r\nIn north-west Rum the Canna Lava Formation consists of four distinct members: the Lower Fionchra Member, Upper Fionchra Member, Guirdil Member, and Orval Member."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL2> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Basalt and trace conglomerate and pyroxene-phyric basalt."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL3> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Basalt and trace conglomerate and feldspar-phyric basalt."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL4> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Feldspar-phyric hawaiite with subsidiary conglomerate and hawaiite and trace basalt."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL5> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Feldspar-phyric hawaiite and trace hawaiite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CNAL6> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Basaltic-andesite and trace conglomerate."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DBLB> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Disturbed Blackheath Beds is regarded as a lithological variant of the Clay-with-flints Formation (McMillan et al., 2011)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/GUIRD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Pyroxene-plagioclase-phyric andesite with subsidiary conglomerate."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LFION> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Olivine-phyric hawaiite with subsidiary conglomerate and trace olivine-basalt."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ORVAL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Mugearite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SEIG> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Porphyritic-rhyolitic pitchstone and trace ash, conglomerate and pitchstone."@en .
